{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba .claude/commands/wf/execute-story.md | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tdescription: Execute one woof story end-to-end (Stage 5 inner sequence). Invoked as a cld -p subprocess by 'just wf-run'. Produces executor_result.json and exits 0; the driver verifies and commits.\n     3\tallowed-tools: Bash(just:*), Bash(./woof/bin/woof:*), Bash(git:*), Bash(test:*), Bash(ls:*), Bash(cat:*), Bash(grep:*), Bash(jq:*), Bash(rg:*), Read, Edit, Write, Glob, Grep\n     4\targument-hint: \"<E<N>> <S<k>>\"\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t# /wf:execute-story — Stage 5 inner sequence (executor role)\n     8\t\n     9\tYou are the story-executor. The `wf-run` driver spawned you to produce a staged diff. You do not verify, commit, or write gate YAML — those belong to the driver. Your contract ends when you write `executor_result.json` and exit 0.\n    10\t\n    11\t`$ARGUMENTS` resolves to `<E<N>> <S<k>>`.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Bootstrap\n    14\t\n    15\tRead in order:\n    16\t\n    17\t1. `.woof/.current-epic` — verify the epic id\n    18\t2. `.woof/epics/E<N>/plan.json` — find your story by id\n    19\t3. `.woof/epics/E<N>/EPIC.md` — front-matter for outcomes / contract decisions referenced by your story\n    20\t4. `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md` — project conventions\n    21\t\n    22\t## Inner sequence\n    23\t\n    24\t1. **Code.** Edit only files matching `story.paths[]` (git-pathspec globs). Files outside that set are a scope violation — if you cannot complete the story within scope, go to step 5 (abort).\n    25\t2. **Tests.** Add or modify tests asserting `story.satisfies[]` outcomes. Each `O<n>` in `satisfies[]` must be referenced (literal `O<n>` token, word-boundary anchored) by at least one test in the diff.\n    26\t3. **Refactor.** Tighten only if it does not widen the diff beyond `paths[]`.\n    27\t4. **Continuous quality gate.** Run the quality-gate command from `.woof/quality-gates.toml` until it exits 0. This is a precondition — do not proceed until the gate is green.\n    28\t5. **Codex critique.** Dispatch:\n    29\t\n    30\t   ```\n    31\t   ./woof/bin/woof dispatch codex --role critiquer --epic <N> --story <Sk> \\\n    32\t       --prompt-file woof/playbooks/critique/story.md\n    33\t   ```\n    34\t\n    35\t   The critique writes `.woof/epics/E<N>/critique/story-S<k>.md`. Read the `severity` field. If `severity: blocker`, proceed to **abort path** (step 7b).\n    36\t\n    37\t6. **Stage the commit transaction.** `git add` all paths matching `story.paths[]` PLUS:\n    38\t   - `.woof/epics/E<N>/plan.json`\n    39\t   - `.woof/epics/E<N>/critique/story-S<k>.md`\n    40\t   - `.woof/epics/E<N>/epic.jsonl`\n    41\t   - `.woof/epics/E<N>/dispatch.jsonl`\n    42\t   - `.woof/epics/E<N>/audit/`\n    43\t\n    44\t   Update `plan.json` story status to `done` and append `story_completed` to `epic.jsonl` before staging.\n    45\t\n    46\t7. **Write `executor_result.json`** at `.woof/epics/E<N>/executor_result.json` and exit 0.\n    47\t\n    48\t   **a. Normal path** (diff staged, critique not blocker):\n    49\t   ```json\n    50\t   {\n    51\t     \"epic_id\": <N>,\n    52\t     \"story_id\": \"<Sk>\",\n    53\t     \"outcome\": \"staged_for_verification\",\n    54\t     \"commit_body\": \"<one-paragraph summary of what was implemented>\",\n    55\t     \"position\": null\n    56\t   }\n    57\t   ```\n    58\t\n    59\t   **b. Abort path** (critique blocker, or scope violation, or cannot proceed):\n    60\t   ```json\n    61\t   {\n    62\t     \"epic_id\": <N>,\n    63\t     \"story_id\": \"<Sk>\",\n    64\t     \"outcome\": \"aborted_with_position\",\n    65\t     \"commit_body\": null,\n    66\t     \"position\": \"<prose: what the critique found, why you halted, recommended resolution>\"\n    67\t   }\n    68\t   ```\n    69\t   Do NOT stage any diff when aborting. The driver reads `position` and writes a story gate.\n    70\t\n    71\t   **c. Empty diff path** (quality gate green but diff is empty):\n    72\t   ```json\n    73\t   {\n    74\t     \"epic_id\": <N>,\n    75\t     \"story_id\": \"<Sk>\",\n    76\t     \"outcome\": \"empty_diff\",\n    77\t     \"commit_body\": null,\n    78\t     \"position\": \"<prose: which earlier story already realised this outcome, or why the diff is legitimately empty>\"\n    79\t   }\n    80\t   ```\n    81\t\n    82\t## Subprocess discipline\n    83\t\n    84\t- **No conversation.** You are running headless.\n    85\t- **No interactive prompts.** All decisions derive from filesystem state and schemas.\n    86\t- **No off-spec excursions.** If you cannot complete the story within scope, write `executor_result.json` with `outcome: aborted_with_position` and exit 0.\n    87\t- **Write executor_result.json once.** Atomic write: write to a `.tmp` suffix, then rename.\n    88\t- **Atomic writes for `plan.json` / `epic.jsonl`.** Use tmp-file + `mv` for `plan.json`; append-mode for `epic.jsonl`.\n    89\t\n    90\t## Exit codes\n    91\t\n    92\t- `0` — `executor_result.json` written; driver reads it and proceeds.\n    93\t- `non-zero` — crash (no `executor_result.json`); driver writes a crash gate automatically.\n    94\t\n    95\tDo not exit 0 without writing `executor_result.json`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
